module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.ImmersionCotangent
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpaceChartRatio.Basic

/-!
# The evaluation `V → ℒ_x/𝔪_x²ℒ_x` of an immersion is surjective

Let `X` be a scheme over a field `k`, let `ℒ` be an invertible `𝒪_X`-module and let
`s₀, …, sₙ` be global sections generating it, the images under `ψ : V → Γ(X, ℒ)` of a basis of a
`k`-vector space `V`. [Stacks, Tag 0FCY] attaches to this datum a morphism
`φ_{ℒ,ψ} : X ⟶ 𝐏(V)`. The proof of [Stacks, Tag 0FD6] asserts, with the words "(small detail
omitted)", that at a closed point `x` of `X` the evaluation

`V ⟶ ℒ_x/𝔪_x²ℒ_x`

is surjective when `φ_{ℒ,ψ}` is an immersion. This file proves that.

## The argument

Pick `i` with `x ∈ X_{sᵢ}`, so that the germ of `sᵢ` is a basis of `ℒ_x`
(`Stacks.SectionProduct.mem_nonvanishingLocus_iff_generates`) and `ℒ_x` is identified with
`𝒪_{X,x}`, the germ of `s_j` corresponding to the germ of the ratio `s_j/sᵢ`.

Over `𝐏(V)` the point `φ(x)` lies in the standard chart `D₊(Tᵢ)`, whose coordinate ring is the
polynomial ring `k[Y_j : j ≠ i]`, and `φ` pulls `Y_j` back to `s_j/sᵢ`
(`Stacks.ProjectiveSpaceChartRatio.chartPullback_eq`). Writing `c_j ∈ k` for the value of
`s_j/sᵢ` at `x` — this is where `x` must be a `k`-rational point — the ideal generated by the
`Y_j - c_j` is a *maximal* ideal of `k[Y_j : j ≠ i]` contained in the prime of `φ(x)`, hence
equal to it. The stalk of `𝐏(V)` at `φ(x)` is the localization of the chart ring at that prime
(`AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen.isLocalization_stalk`), so `𝔪_{φ(x)}` is generated by the germs
of the `Y_j - c_j`; and `φ` being an immersion is surjective on stalks, so `𝔪_x` is generated by
the germs of the `s_j/sᵢ - c_j`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.span_image_stalkMap_eq_maximalIdeal`).

A local ring whose maximal ideal is generated by finitely many elements and whose residue field
is the base field has `R/𝔪²` spanned over that field by `1` and those generators; transporting
back along the basis `sᵢ` of `ℒ_x` gives the assertion.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.ImmersionEvaluationSurjective.baseGerm`: the structure morphism `k → 𝒪_{X,x}`.
* `Stacks.ImmersionEvaluationSurjective.maximalSqSmul`: the submodule `𝔪_x²·ℒ_x` of `ℒ_x`.

## Main results

* `MvPolynomial.isMaximal_span_X_sub_C`: the ideal generated by the `X j - c j` is maximal.
* `IsLocalRing.exists_sub_sum_mem_sq`: `R/𝔪²` is spanned over the base field by `1` and a
  generating family of `𝔪`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen.germ_mem_maximalIdeal_iff` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen.span_image_germ_eq_maximalIdeal`: the prime of a point of an
  affine open, read in the stalk.
* `Stacks.ImmersionEvaluationSurjective.span_germ_ratio_sub_eq_maximalIdeal`: **`𝔪_x` is
  generated by the germs of the `s_j/sᵢ - c_j`.**
* `Stacks.ImmersionEvaluationSurjective.exists_coeff_sub_sum_smul_germ_mem` and
  `Stacks.ImmersionEvaluationSurjective.surjective_evalQuotient`: **the evaluation is
  surjective onto `ℒ_x/𝔪_x²ℒ_x`.**
* `Stacks.ImmersionEvaluationSurjective.surjective_evalQuotient_of_isImmersion`: the same with
  the source's own hypothesis, that the Tag 0FCY morphism `φ_{ℒ,ψ} : X ⟶ 𝐏(V)` is an immersion.

## The rationality hypothesis

The statement is false without it: for `X` the spectrum of a cubic extension of `k`, a closed
point of the affine line, the evaluation has a two-dimensional image in a three-dimensional
target. The hypothesis appears below as

`∀ a : 𝒪_{X,x}, ∃ c : k, a - baseGerm f x c ∈ 𝔪_x`,

that is, `k → κ(x)` is surjective. In the proof of Tag 0FD6 the base field has already been
enlarged to an algebraically closed one and `x` is a closed point of a scheme of finite type
over it, so the hypothesis holds; it is discharged in that form in the sibling file
`ClosedPoint.lean`.

## Surjectivity, in coordinates

`ℒ_x` is a module over `𝒪_{X,x}`, not over `k`, and no `k`-module structure on it is introduced
here. "The evaluation `V → ℒ_x/𝔪_x²ℒ_x` is surjective" is therefore stated in the coordinates
the basis of `V` supplies: the map sending a tuple `c : Fin (n+1) → k` to the class of
`∑ⱼ c_j · (sⱼ)_x` is surjective onto `ℒ_x/𝔪_x²ℒ_x`.

**No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached.** Nothing below is the assertion of a tag: this is the
proof of a step the source omits inside the proof of Tag 0FD6, and Tag 0FCY already carries its
registrations at `AlgebraicGeometry.toProjectiveSpaceOfModule_comp_toSpec` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.toProjectiveSpaceOfModule_comp_basisProjectiveSpaceIso_inv`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FD6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FD6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FCY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FCY)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory IsLocalRing
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjPolyChart
open Stacks.ModuleStalk Stacks.ProjectiveFromSections Stacks.ProjectiveSpaceChartRatio

universe u

/-! ### The maximal ideal of a polynomial ring at a point of the base field -/

namespace MvPolynomial

variable {ι k : Type*} [CommRing k]

/-- Every polynomial is congruent to its value at `c` modulo the ideal generated by the
`X j - c j`. -/
theorem sub_C_eval_mem_span_X_sub_C (c : ι → k) (p : MvPolynomial ι k) :
    p - C (eval c p) ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range fun j => X j - C (c j)) := by
  induction p using MvPolynomial.induction_on with
  | C a => simp
  | add p q hp hq =>
      have h : p + q - C (eval c (p + q)) = p - C (eval c p) + (q - C (eval c q)) := by
        rw [map_add, map_add]; ring
      rw [h]; exact Ideal.add_mem _ hp hq
  | mul_X p j hp =>
      have h : p * X j - C (eval c (p * X j)) =
          p * (X j - C (c j)) + (p - C (eval c p)) * C (c j) := by
        rw [map_mul, eval_X, map_mul]; ring
      rw [h]
      exact Ideal.add_mem _ (Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (Ideal.subset_span ⟨j, rfl⟩))
        (Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ hp)

/-- The kernel of evaluation at `c` is generated by the `X j - c j`. -/
theorem ker_eval_eq_span_X_sub_C (c : ι → k) :
    RingHom.ker (eval c) = Ideal.span (Set.range fun j => X j - C (c j)) := by
  refine le_antisymm (fun p hp => ?_) (Ideal.span_le.2 ?_)
  · have h := sub_C_eval_mem_span_X_sub_C c p
    rwa [RingHom.mem_ker.1 hp, map_zero, sub_zero] at h
  · rintro _ ⟨j, rfl⟩
    simp [RingHom.mem_ker]

/-- **The ideal generated by the `X j - c j` is maximal** when the `c j` lie in a field: it is
the kernel of evaluation at `c`, a surjection onto the field. -/
theorem isMaximal_span_X_sub_C {k : Type*} [Field k] (c : ι → k) :
    (Ideal.span (Set.range fun j => (X j - C (c j) : MvPolynomial ι k))).IsMaximal := by
  rw [← ker_eval_eq_span_X_sub_C]
  exact RingHom.ker_isMaximal_of_surjective (eval c) fun a => ⟨C a, by simp⟩

end MvPolynomial

/-! ### Spanning the square quotient of a local ring -/

/-- **A generating family of the maximal ideal spans `R/𝔪²` over the base field, together with
`1`.** Let `β : k → R` be a homomorphism from a field into a local ring whose composite with the
residue map is surjective, and let `y` be a finite family generating `𝔪`. Then every element of
`R` is, modulo `𝔪²`, a `k`-combination of `1` and the `y j`. -/
theorem IsLocalRing.exists_sub_sum_mem_sq {k R : Type*} [Field k] [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    (β : k →+* R) (hβ : ∀ a : R, ∃ c : k, a - β c ∈ maximalIdeal R)
    {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] (y : ι → R) (hy : Ideal.span (Set.range y) = maximalIdeal R)
    (a : R) :
    ∃ (c : k) (d : ι → k), a - β c - ∑ j, β (d j) * y j ∈ maximalIdeal R ^ 2 := by
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hβ a
  rw [← hy] at hc
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := Submodule.mem_span_range_iff_exists_fun R |>.1 hc
  choose d hd using fun j => hβ (u j)
  refine ⟨c, d, ?_⟩
  have hyj : ∀ j, y j ∈ maximalIdeal R := by
    intro j
    rw [← hy]
    exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨j, rfl⟩
  have key : a - β c - ∑ j, β (d j) * y j = ∑ j, (u j - β (d j)) * y j := by
    rw [← hu, ← Finset.sum_sub_distrib]
    exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => by rw [smul_eq_mul, sub_mul]
  rw [key, pow_two]
  exact Submodule.sum_mem _ fun j _ => Ideal.mul_mem_mul (hd j) (hyj j)

/-! ### The maximal ideal of a stalk, read on an affine open -/

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (x : X) (hx : x ∈ U)

/-- The germ map at `x` pulls the maximal ideal of the stalk back to the prime of `x` and pushes
that prime forward onto it, since the stalk is the localization at that prime. -/
private theorem comap_map_germ_maximalIdeal :
    (maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x)).comap (X.presheaf.germ U x hx).hom =
        (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hx⟩).asIdeal ∧
      (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hx⟩).asIdeal.map (X.presheaf.germ U x hx).hom =
        maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) := by
  let : Algebra Γ(X, U) (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
    TopCat.Presheaf.algebra_section_stalk X.presheaf ⟨x, hx⟩
  have : IsLocalization.AtPrime (X.presheaf.stalk x) (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hx⟩).asIdeal :=
    hU.isLocalization_stalk ⟨x, hx⟩
  exact ⟨IsLocalization.AtPrime.under_maximalIdeal _ _,
    IsLocalization.AtPrime.map_eq_maximalIdeal _ _⟩

include hU in
/-- **A section of an affine open lies in the prime of a point exactly when its germ there is a
nonunit**: the stalk is the localization of the sections at that prime. -/
theorem germ_mem_maximalIdeal_iff (b : Γ(X, U)) :
    (X.presheaf.germ U x hx).hom b ∈ maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) ↔
      b ∈ (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hx⟩).asIdeal := by
  rw [← (hU.comap_map_germ_maximalIdeal x hx).1, Ideal.mem_comap]

include hU in
/-- **A generating family of the prime of a point generates the maximal ideal of the stalk.** -/
theorem span_image_germ_eq_maximalIdeal {T : Set Γ(X, U)}
    (hT : Ideal.span T = (hU.primeIdealOf ⟨x, hx⟩).asIdeal) :
    Ideal.span ((X.presheaf.germ U x hx).hom '' T) = maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) := by
  rw [← Ideal.map_span, hT]
  exact (hU.comap_map_germ_maximalIdeal x hx).2

end AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen

/-! ### Germs of pulled-back sections -/

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- The germ of a section pulled back along `g` is the image under the stalk map of its germ. -/
theorem germ_appLE {X Y : Scheme.{u}} (g : X ⟶ Y) {W : Y.Opens} {U : X.Opens}
    (e : U ≤ g ⁻¹ᵁ W) (x : X) (hx : x ∈ U) (hgx : g x ∈ W) (b : Γ(Y, W)) :
    (X.presheaf.germ U x hx).hom (g.appLE W U e b) =
      (g.stalkMap x).hom ((Y.presheaf.germ W (g x) hgx).hom b) := by
  rw [Scheme.Hom.germ_stalkMap_apply, Scheme.Hom.appLE,
    CategoryTheory.ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply]

end AlgebraicGeometry

/-! ### The maximal ideal of the stalk, generated by the ratios -/

namespace Stacks.ImmersionEvaluationSurjective

attribute [local instance] MvPolynomial.gradedAlgebra

variable {k : Type u} [Field k] {n : ℕ} {X : Scheme.{u}} {L : X.Modules}
  [Stacks.Ample.IsInvertibleModule X L] (s : Fin (n + 1) → Γ(L, ⊤))
  (hs : GeneratesStalks s) (f : X ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of k))

/-- **The structure morphism of `X` over `k`, read in the stalk at a point.** -/
def baseGerm (f : X ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of k)) (x : X) : k →+* X.presheaf.stalk x :=
  (X.presheaf.Γgerm x).hom.comp
    (f.appTop.hom.comp (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of k)).inv.hom)

/-- The germ of the chart's `k`-algebra structure map is the structure map in the stalk. -/
theorem germ_chartBaseHom (i : Fin (n + 1)) {x : X} (hx : x ∈ nvCover s i) (r : k) :
    (X.presheaf.germ (nvCover s i) x hx).hom (chartBaseHom s f i r) = baseGerm f x r := by
  have h1 : chartBaseHom s f i r =
      f.appLE ⊤ (nvCover s i) le_top ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of k)).inv r) := rfl
  have h2 : baseGerm f x r =
      (X.presheaf.Γgerm x).hom (f.appTop ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of k)).inv r)) := rfl
  have h3 : f.appLE ⊤ (nvCover s i) le_top ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of k)).inv r) =
      X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : nvCover s i ≤ ⊤)).op
        (f.appTop ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (CommRingCat.of k)).inv r)) := rfl
  rw [h1, h2, h3, TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply]
  rfl

/-- **The maximal ideal of `𝒪_{X,x}` is generated by the germs of the `s_j/s_i - c_j`.**

Here `x` lies in the nonvanishing open of `sᵢ` and the `c_j ∈ k` are scalars with
`(s_j/s_i)(x) = c_j`. The morphism to projective space being surjective on stalks, the maximal
ideal upstairs is generated by the chart coordinates `Y_j - c_j`, and
`Stacks.ProjectiveSpaceChartRatio.chartPullback_eq` says those pull back to the `s_j/s_i - c_j`.
-/
theorem span_germ_ratio_sub_eq_maximalIdeal
    (hφ : SurjectiveOnStalks (toPolynomialModel s hs f))
    {x : X} {i : Fin (n + 1)} (hx : x ∈ nvCover s i)
    (c : {j : Fin (n + 1) // j ≠ i} → k)
    (hc : ∀ j, (X.presheaf.germ (nvCover s i) x hx).hom (ratio s i j.1)
        - baseGerm f x (c j) ∈ maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x)) :
    Ideal.span (Set.range fun j : {j : Fin (n + 1) // j ≠ i} =>
        (X.presheaf.germ (nvCover s i) x hx).hom (ratio s i j.1) - baseGerm f x (c j)) =
      maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) := by
  have := hφ
  have e : nvCover s i ≤ toPolynomialModel s hs f ⁻¹ᵁ
      AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen (polyGrading k n) (MvPolynomial.X i) :=
    nvCover_le_preimage_basicOpen_toPolynomialModel s hs f i
  have hWaff : IsAffineOpen
      (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen (polyGrading k n) (MvPolynomial.X i)) :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.isAffineOpen_basicOpen _ _ (X_mem_one k n i) Nat.one_pos
  have hφx : toPolynomialModel s hs f x ∈
      AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen (polyGrading k n) (MvPolynomial.X i) := e hx
  -- the chart ring map `k[Y_j : j ≠ i] → Γ(ℙⁿ_k, D₊(Tᵢ))`
  let cs : MvPolynomial {j : Fin (n + 1) // j ≠ i} k →+*
      Γ(AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading k n),
        AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen (polyGrading k n) (MvPolynomial.X i)) :=
    (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayToSection (polyGrading k n) (MvPolynomial.X i)).hom.comp
      (chartHom k n i)
  have hiso : IsIso (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayToSection (polyGrading k n)
      (MvPolynomial.X i)) :=
    (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpenIsoAway (polyGrading k n) (MvPolynomial.X i)
      (X_mem_one k n i) Nat.one_pos).isIso_hom
  have hcs : Function.Surjective cs :=
    (CategoryTheory.ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso
      (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.awayToSection (polyGrading k n) (MvPolynomial.X i))).2.comp
      (chartHom_surjective k n i)
  let gen : {j : Fin (n + 1) // j ≠ i} → MvPolynomial {j : Fin (n + 1) // j ≠ i} k :=
    fun j => MvPolynomial.X j - MvPolynomial.C (c j)
  have hgen : ∀ j, gen j = MvPolynomial.X j - MvPolynomial.C (c j) := fun _ => rfl
  -- the chart identification: `Y_j - c_j` pulls back to `s_j/s_i - c_j`
  have hkey : ∀ j, (X.presheaf.germ (nvCover s i) x hx).hom
      ((toPolynomialModel s hs f).appLE _ (nvCover s i) e (cs (gen j))) =
      (X.presheaf.germ (nvCover s i) x hx).hom (ratio s i j.1) - baseGerm f x (c j) := by
    intro j
    have h1 : (toPolynomialModel s hs f).appLE _ (nvCover s i) e (cs (gen j)) =
        chartPullback s hs f i (gen j) := rfl
    rw [h1, chartPullback_eq s hs f i, hgen j, map_sub, MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_X',
      MvPolynomial.eval₂Hom_C, map_sub, germ_chartBaseHom s f i hx (c j)]
  -- the generators lie in the prime of `φ x`
  have hmem : ∀ j, cs (gen j) ∈ (hWaff.primeIdealOf ⟨_, hφx⟩).asIdeal := by
    intro j
    rw [← AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen.germ_mem_maximalIdeal_iff hWaff _ hφx,
      ← IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal_comap ((toPolynomialModel s hs f).stalkMap x).hom,
      Ideal.mem_comap, ← germ_appLE (toPolynomialModel s hs f) e x hx hφx, hkey j]
    exact hc j
  -- and generate it, because they generate a maximal ideal downstairs
  have hq : (hWaff.primeIdealOf ⟨_, hφx⟩).asIdeal = Ideal.span (cs '' Set.range gen) := by
    have hJ : (Ideal.span (Set.range gen)).IsMaximal := MvPolynomial.isMaximal_span_X_sub_C c
    have hle : Ideal.span (Set.range gen) ≤
        (hWaff.primeIdealOf ⟨_, hφx⟩).asIdeal.comap cs := by
      rw [Ideal.span_le]
      rintro _ ⟨j, rfl⟩
      exact hmem j
    have hne : (hWaff.primeIdealOf ⟨_, hφx⟩).asIdeal.comap cs ≠ ⊤ := by
      intro h
      refine (hWaff.primeIdealOf ⟨_, hφx⟩).isPrime.ne_top ((Ideal.eq_top_iff_one _).2 ?_)
      simpa using (Ideal.eq_top_iff_one _).1 h
    rw [← Ideal.map_span, hJ.eq_of_le hne hle, Ideal.map_comap_of_surjective cs hcs]
  -- transport along the germ and the stalk map
  have hmax := hWaff.span_image_germ_eq_maximalIdeal _ hφx hq.symm
  have hfinal := AlgebraicGeometry.span_image_stalkMap_eq_maximalIdeal
    (toPolynomialModel s hs f) x hmax
  rw [← hfinal, Set.image_image, Set.image_image, ← Set.range_comp]
  refine congrArg Ideal.span (congrArg Set.range (funext fun j => ?_))
  rw [Function.comp_apply, ← hkey j, germ_appLE (toPolynomialModel s hs f) e x hx hφx]

/-! ### Surjectivity of the evaluation on the stalk of `ℒ` -/

/-- The submodule `𝔪_x² · ℒ_x` of the stalk of `ℒ` at `x`. -/
def maximalSqSmul (L : X.Modules) (x : X) :
    Submodule (X.presheaf.stalk x) (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) L.presheaf x) :=
  maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) ^ 2 • ⊤

/-- The germ of `s_j` is the germ of the ratio `s_j/s_i` times the germ of `s_i`. -/
theorem germ_ratio_smul_Γgerm (i j : Fin (n + 1)) {x : X} (hx : x ∈ nvCover s i) :
    (X.presheaf.germ (nvCover s i) x hx).hom (ratio s i j) •
        (L.presheaf.Γgerm x).hom (s i) = (L.presheaf.Γgerm x).hom (s j) := by
  have hres : ∀ t : Fin (n + 1),
      (L.presheaf.germ (nvCover s i) x hx).hom (resT (nvCover s i) (s t)) =
        (L.presheaf.Γgerm x).hom (s t) := fun t =>
    TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply L.presheaf (homOfLE (le_top : nvCover s i ≤ ⊤)) x hx (s t)
  have h := congrArg (L.presheaf.germ (nvCover s i) x hx).hom (ratio_smul s i j)
  rwa [Stacks.ModuleStalk.germ_smul, hres, hres] at h

/-- **The evaluation at `x` of a generating linear system defining an immersion is
surjective onto `ℒ_x/𝔪_x²ℒ_x`**, in the coordinates of the family `s`: every germ is, modulo
`𝔪_x²ℒ_x`, a `k`-combination of the germs of the `sⱼ`.

The hypothesis `hres` says that `x` is a `k`-rational point, which is the situation of
[Stacks, Tag 0FD6]: there the base field has already been enlarged to an algebraically closed
one and `x` is a closed point of a scheme of finite type over it. -/
theorem exists_coeff_sub_sum_smul_germ_mem
    (hφ : SurjectiveOnStalks (toPolynomialModel s hs f)) {x : X}
    (hres : ∀ a : X.presheaf.stalk x, ∃ c : k,
      a - baseGerm f x c ∈ maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x))
    (w : TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) L.presheaf x) :
    ∃ c : Fin (n + 1) → k,
      w - ∑ j, baseGerm f x (c j) • (L.presheaf.Γgerm x).hom (s j) ∈ maximalSqSmul L x := by
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := exists_mem_nvCover_of_generatesStalks s hs x
  choose c₀ hc₀ using fun j : {j : Fin (n + 1) // j ≠ i} =>
    hres ((X.presheaf.germ (nvCover s i) x hi).hom (ratio s i j.1))
  have hm := span_germ_ratio_sub_eq_maximalIdeal s hs f hφ hi c₀ hc₀
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := (Stacks.SectionProduct.mem_nonvanishingLocus_iff_generates L (s i) x).1 hi w
  obtain ⟨a, d, had⟩ := IsLocalRing.exists_sub_sum_mem_sq (baseGerm f x) hres
    (fun j : {j : Fin (n + 1) // j ≠ i} =>
      (X.presheaf.germ (nvCover s i) x hi).hom (ratio s i j.1) - baseGerm f x (c₀ j)) hm r
  classical
  refine ⟨fun t => if h : t = i then a - ∑ j : {j : Fin (n + 1) // j ≠ i}, d j * c₀ j
    else d ⟨t, h⟩, ?_⟩
  have hsplit : ∑ t, baseGerm f x
        (if h : t = i then a - ∑ j : {j : Fin (n + 1) // j ≠ i}, d j * c₀ j else d ⟨t, h⟩) •
        (L.presheaf.Γgerm x).hom (s t) =
      (baseGerm f x a +
        ∑ j : {j : Fin (n + 1) // j ≠ i}, baseGerm f x (d j) *
          ((X.presheaf.germ (nvCover s i) x hi).hom (ratio s i j.1) - baseGerm f x (c₀ j))) •
        (L.presheaf.Γgerm x).hom (s i) := by
    have hterm : ∀ j : {j : Fin (n + 1) // j ≠ i},
        baseGerm f x (if h : j.1 = i then a - ∑ j : {j : Fin (n + 1) // j ≠ i}, d j * c₀ j
            else d ⟨j.1, h⟩) • (L.presheaf.Γgerm x).hom (s j.1) =
          (baseGerm f x (d j) *
            (X.presheaf.germ (nvCover s i) x hi).hom (ratio s i j.1)) •
            (L.presheaf.Γgerm x).hom (s i) := by
      intro j
      rw [dite_eq_right j.2, ← germ_ratio_smul_Γgerm s i j.1 hi, smul_smul]
    have hi0 : (if h : i = i then a - ∑ j : {j : Fin (n + 1) // j ≠ i}, d j * c₀ j
        else d ⟨i, h⟩) = a - ∑ j : {j : Fin (n + 1) // j ≠ i}, d j * c₀ j := dite_eq_left rfl
    have hcoef : baseGerm f x (a - ∑ j : {j : Fin (n + 1) // j ≠ i}, d j * c₀ j) +
        ∑ j : {j : Fin (n + 1) // j ≠ i}, baseGerm f x (d j) *
          (X.presheaf.germ (nvCover s i) x hi).hom (ratio s i j.1) =
        baseGerm f x a +
          ∑ j : {j : Fin (n + 1) // j ≠ i}, baseGerm f x (d j) *
            ((X.presheaf.germ (nvCover s i) x hi).hom (ratio s i j.1) -
              baseGerm f x (c₀ j)) := by
      rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl fun (j : {j : Fin (n + 1) // j ≠ i}) _ => mul_sub
          (baseGerm f x (d j)) ((X.presheaf.germ (nvCover s i) x hi).hom (ratio s i j.1))
          (baseGerm f x (c₀ j)),
        Finset.sum_sub_distrib, map_sub, map_sum,
        Finset.sum_congr rfl fun (j : {j : Fin (n + 1) // j ≠ i}) _ =>
          map_mul (baseGerm f x) (d j) (c₀ j)]
      ring
    rw [Fintype.sum_eq_add_sum_compl i, hi0,
      Finset.sum_subtype (p := fun t : Fin (n + 1) => t ≠ i) ({i} : Finset (Fin (n + 1)))ᶜ
        (fun t => by simp) _,
      Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => hterm j, ← Finset.sum_smul, ← add_smul, hcoef]
  rw [hsplit, hr, ← sub_smul]
  refine Submodule.smul_mem_smul ?_ Submodule.mem_top
  rw [← sub_sub]
  exact had

/-- **The evaluation `ev_x` is surjective onto `ℒ_x/𝔪_x²ℒ_x`**, read in the coordinates of the
family `s`: the map sending a tuple of scalars to the class of the corresponding combination of
the germs of the `sⱼ` is surjective. -/
theorem surjective_evalQuotient
    (hφ : SurjectiveOnStalks (toPolynomialModel s hs f)) {x : X}
    (hres : ∀ a : X.presheaf.stalk x, ∃ c : k,
      a - baseGerm f x c ∈ maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x)) :
    Function.Surjective fun c : Fin (n + 1) → k =>
      Submodule.Quotient.mk (p := maximalSqSmul L x)
        (∑ j, baseGerm f x (c j) • (L.presheaf.Γgerm x).hom (s j)) := by
  intro q
  obtain ⟨w, rfl⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective (maximalSqSmul L x) q
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := exists_coeff_sub_sum_smul_germ_mem s hs f hφ hres w
  exact ⟨c, ((Submodule.Quotient.eq _).2 hc).symm⟩

/-! ### The hypothesis of the source: `φ_{ℒ,ψ}` is an immersion -/

variable {V : Type u} [AddCommGroup V] [Module k V]

/-- The morphism of [Stacks, Tag 0FCY] and the morphism read in the polynomial model differ by
isomorphisms, so an immersion `φ_{ℒ,ψ}` makes the latter surjective on stalks. -/
theorem surjectiveOnStalks_toPolynomialModel (b : Module.Basis (Fin (n + 1)) k V)
    [IsImmersion (AlgebraicGeometry.toProjectiveSpaceOfModule b s hs f)] :
    SurjectiveOnStalks (toPolynomialModel s hs f) := by
  rw [← toProjectiveSpaceOfModule_comp_eq_toPolynomialModel s hs f b]
  infer_instance

/-- **The detail [Stacks, Tag 0FD6] omits.** Let `ψ : V → Γ(X, ℒ)` send a basis of `V` to a
family `s₀, …, sₙ` generating the invertible module `ℒ`, and suppose the morphism
`φ_{ℒ,ψ} : X ⟶ 𝐏(V)` of [Stacks, Tag 0FCY] is an immersion. Then at a `k`-rational point `x` the
evaluation

`V ⟶ ℒ_x/𝔪_x²ℒ_x`

is surjective: every germ is, modulo `𝔪_x²ℒ_x`, a `k`-combination of the germs of the `sⱼ`,
which are the images of the basis of `V`. -/
theorem surjective_evalQuotient_of_isImmersion (b : Module.Basis (Fin (n + 1)) k V)
    [IsImmersion (AlgebraicGeometry.toProjectiveSpaceOfModule b s hs f)] {x : X}
    (hres : ∀ a : X.presheaf.stalk x, ∃ c : k,
      a - baseGerm f x c ∈ maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x)) :
    Function.Surjective fun c : Fin (n + 1) → k =>
      Submodule.Quotient.mk (p := maximalSqSmul L x)
        (∑ j, baseGerm f x (c j) • (L.presheaf.Γgerm x).hom (s j)) :=
  surjective_evalQuotient s hs f (surjectiveOnStalks_toPolynomialModel s hs f b) hres

end Stacks.ImmersionEvaluationSurjective

end
